// complementary relations, the bare closer, and a later second analysis
let x, y be reals. wts min(x, y) <= max(x, y)
case x <= y. then min(x, y) = x <= y = max(x, y).
case x > y. then min(x, y) = y < x = max(x, y).
these cases are exhaustive.

next we show |x - y| = max(x, y) - min(x, y).
case 1 x <= y. then |x - y| = y - x.
case 2 x > y. then |x - y| = x - y.
in both cases, |x - y| = max(x, y) - min(x, y).
qed
